      {
        "id": 21443,
        "name": "Hedge",
        "username": "Hedge",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/e95f7d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-08-17T09:04:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Adam&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Adam\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah, I see what you mean. A target is anything with hit points, so you can target other heroes if you see the need to. The only thing that prevents what you’re saying from working is that if you’re using Imbued Fire, it converts ALL damage to fire damage, including the damage Absolute Zero deals to himself. As such, he can’t deal himself cold damage, so he can’t heal. If you manage to do fire damage to him outside of Imbued Fire, he can heal that back, but there’s no way to match that level of damage output with him.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I was so Close. I still think there is a way with Ra and AZ, If Ra can do more, but not over the 28 limitation per strike, than Tachyon. Then AZ can do more than Ra if Ra were to inflict the damage on AZ instead of the Villian.</p>",
